diff --git a/docs/pages/fatras_decays.md b/docs/pages/fatras_decays.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..1d263e1eef
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/pages/fatras_decays.md
@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@
+# Native Fatras decays {#fatras_decays}
+
+`ActsFatras::NativeDecay` supplies a small decay model without a Geant4 runtime
+dependency. It uses the Fatras proper-time scheduling and recursive daughter
+transport. It is opt-in in Examples:
+
+```python
+addFatras(
+    sequencer, trackingGeometry, field, randomNumbers,
+    enableDecays=True,
+    pMin=0.1 * acts.UnitConstants.GeV,
+    pTMin=0.05 * acts.UnitConstants.GeV,
+)
+```
+
+In C++, set `FatrasSimulation::Config::enableDecays = true`. The default is false.
+The Python `enableDecays` option is independent of `enableInteractions`, so
+vacuum decays can be studied with material interactions disabled. A supplied
+hadronic table can be used with the native decay model. Charged particles remain
+stable in this first implementation.
+
+## Physics scope
+
+| Parent | Mean lifetime | Retained channels | Charged-channel probability |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| K-short | 0.8954e-10 s | pi+ pi-, pi0 pi0 | 0.6920 / (0.6920 + 0.3069) |
+| Lambda | 2.617e-10 s | p pi-, n pi0 | 0.641 |
+| anti-Lambda | Same as Lambda | anti-p pi+, anti-n pi0 | 0.641 |
+| pi0 | Prompt at production vertex | gamma gamma | 0 |
+
+Lifetimes and relative V0 channel weights use the PDG 2026
+[K-short listing](https://pdg.lbl.gov/2026/listings/rpp2026-list-K-zero-S.pdf)
+(CPT lifetime fit) and
+[Lambda listing](https://pdg.lbl.gov/2026/listings/rpp2026-list-lambda.pdf).
+Masses and charges use the ACTS particle table; kinematics uses the transported
+parent mass. These are narrow on-shell states, not a model for off-shell decays.
+
+The retained channel weights are normalized to one. Rare semileptonic and
+radiative channels are omitted; this slightly redistributes their probability
+into the retained modes. Inclusive radiation is not generated separately.
+Pi0 decay uses only two photons and omits the Dalitz channel. These are explicit
+tracking approximations, not a complete decay table. Both charged and neutral
+V0 channels are retained to avoid forcing charged-track production.
+
+Remaining proper lifetimes are exponential and added to the initial proper
+age. Directions are isotropic in the parent rest frame, with exact two-body
+kinematics followed by a Lorentz boost. The Lambda model assumes unpolarized
+parents; spin transport, polarization correlations, CP asymmetries, neutral-kaon
+mixing and regeneration are absent. Other species have infinite lifetime.
+All draws use the caller's event RNG; disabled and unsupported particles consume
+no decay random numbers. Reproducibility requires the same random engine,
+standard library and configuration.
+
+## Acceptance and truth
+
+Supported moving neutral decay parents bypass `pMin` when decays are enabled.
+Their rest energy can produce accepted daughters even at low parent momentum.
+The normal `pMin` and charged `pTMin` cuts apply to stable daughters. Upstream
+particle selectors must also retain these neutral parents. Exact zero-momentum
+particles are excluded by the Examples neutral selector: at-rest transport is
+not part of this implementation.
+
+The parent retains its terminal four-momentum and receives
+`SimulationOutcome::Decayed`. Daughters carry `GenerationProcess::eDecay`, the
+parent barcode and the decay space-time position; their own proper ages start
+at zero. Neutral pions from V0 decays remain explicit truth particles and decay
+promptly through the same policy. Photon conversion then uses the existing EM
+model. Below-cut daughters are omitted from the transported output as in the
+existing Fatras selection, so selected output alone need not close four-momentum.
+The hadronic interaction model still folds its own prompt pi0 decays into the
+nuclear vertex; it shares the two-body kinematics utility.
+
+Feed Fatras only particles that still need transport. Configure the event
+generator to leave the desired V0 species undecayed if Fatras should place their
+vertices. If the generator already decays them, supply its final-state daughters
+without also supplying their parents. Examples skips parents explicitly marked
+`Decayed`, but a flat input collection without decay status cannot reveal double
+counting. Native decays do not replace generator decay trees or relocate existing
+daughters. Neutron/antineutron daughters currently have no nuclear interactions.
+
+## Validation
+
+Unit tests check exponential lifetime means and survival probabilities, channel
+fractions, rest-frame angular moments, charge and four-momentum conservation,
+boosts, thresholds, prompt decay and deterministic replay across threads.
+Integration tests compare sampled lifetimes with propagated decay positions and
+times, check world exit, preserve low-momentum parents, and follow charged hits
+and pi0 photon cascades with consistent truth identifiers.
+
+Before judging detector performance, compare dedicated V0 samples and realistic
+events with a documented generator decay policy. Record decay vertices, daughter
+momenta and angles, hits per layer, losses to cuts/navigation, CPU and event tails.
+The unit and synthetic transport tests do not establish full-simulation agreement.
+Geant4 can be an optional reference; it is not needed by the native model.
